          "type": "turn",
          "question": "If a record says \"diabetes with neuropathy\", does the coder need a statement that the diabetes caused the neuropathy?",
          "answer": "The retrieved passages suggest the coder does not need a separate statement linking the diabetes to the neuropathy, but they don't state that rule directly.\n\nThe nervous-system chapter summary says diabetic neuropathy is coded from the diabetes category in the endocrine chapter, not from the polyneuropathy block, \"because the classification presumes the association\" (Chapter 6 summary, ICD-10-CM nervous system). The type 2 diabetes summary says neuropathy, including the polyneuropathy and autonomic forms, is one of the complication subcategories of E11 (Coding type 2 diabetes: E11 and its complication subcategories). Together, these indicate that the pairing of diabetes and neuropathy is presumed in the classification.\n\nThe passages do not say what wording a record needs to link the two, or whether a record that lists them separately would be handled differently. For that, check the current official ICD-10-CM coding guidelines or your organization's coding policy.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
